    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d348">

                <pb facs="0665" n="1319" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg1319"/>

                <head>No. 640.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cadwalader to Aristarchi
                    Bey.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-10-30"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 30,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge with thanks
                    the receipt of your note of the 15th instant, and the school-books therewith
                    transmitted for the library of the Commissioner of Education.</p>
                <p>Pursuant to your request, the expressions of gratitude offered by the minister of
                    public instruction to the Commissioner of Education for the works presented to
                    the former, have been conveyed to him; and application has been made for a
                    collection of the text-books used in the public schools of the United States,
                    which the minister desires.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN L. CADWALADER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                            Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
